th Seo Taiji and Boys, who incorporated rap, rock, and dance elements into Korean popular music.\nModern\u00a0K-pop \"idol\" culture\u00a0began later in the 1990s, as K-pop idol music grew into a\u00a0subculture.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "BTS", "streams": 48996, "best_position": 6}, {"artist": "Agust D", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "CORTIS", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "ENHYPEN", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "ILLIT", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jimin", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jin", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jung Kook", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "LE SSERAFIM", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "NewJeans", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "RM", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "latin": {"genre": "latin", "country_code": "ec", "country_name": "Ecuador", "summary": "Latin American music or Latin music encompasses rhythms and styles originated or related to Latin America and its influence in the United States and several European countries such as Spain or Portugal. Some critics have defined Latin music as an incorporation of four elements: music style, geography, cultural background of the artist and language. The first of those encapsulates all music styles generated from Latin countries, such as salsa, merengue.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "KAROL G", "streams": 152278, "best_position": 1}, {"artist": "Bad Bunny", "streams": 125290, "best_position": 18}, {"artist": "Omar Courtz", "streams": 73385, "best_position": 11}, {"artist": "Romeo Santos", "streams": 55930, "best_position": 43}, {"artist": "J\u00f3sean Log", "streams": 48540, "best_position": 7}, {"artist": "Maluma", "streams": 40051, "best_position": 26}, {"artist": "Rauw Alejandro", "streams": 32642, "best